    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2LjaDJAcqvwjN3vnf8zS33u)_\n\n## Summary\n- Bindings `s-f` (`forward-word`) and `s-b` (`backward-word`) were first added in commit [e53672d](https://github.com/siainbuletin/dotfiles/commit/e53672da955959216b9260d7db6baee6f2956f66), then removed again in this PR.\n- Why removed: `s-b` clashes with bold in Org (`sp-org-base`) and Markdown (`sp-md`). The real problem is that `M-b` (Option+b) does nothing in Sia's Emacs, even though `ns-alternate-modifier` is `meta`. The cause is not found yet.\n- `sp-text-manipulation.org` records the attempt, the reason and the commit link. The tangled `.el` is back to its previous content.\n- No CHANGELOG edit, per the nightly-tidy rule. For the nightly run: the Command word-motion bindings were tried (e53672d) and dropped.\n\n## Testing\nUntested: Emacs does not run in the cloud container.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCG7WRQHXBfHi427t3\n",
